      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MOHEGAN RULER (1) is better than we saw last time out when failing after sitting handy over 1300m here as the race favourite. Back to 1200m looks to hold the key after a good run here two back. Can sit prominently again and land the knockout blow. RAY'S SAUCE (2) missed the placings two runs back then improved last start but found a couple better over 1000m at this track, beaten 4.5 lengths after being prominent at the corner. Looks well placed so expect another big run. BLATANT VIOLATION (6) registered his first win last start over 1406m at Roebourne, getting home by a long neck. Sparingly raced and has more to offer. Re-unites with Austin Galati who was on board last start. Must be respected now that the penny has dropped. CASSENITE (4) has been racing in great heart with two top-three finishes on end, the latest a second over 1300m at Port Hedland when she was handy all the way. Looks well placed so expect another big run. SANCTIONS (8) is next.",
